      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Files",
      "description": "File upload endpoints. All require JWT.\n\nOnly one upload strategy is active at a time — determined by the `FILE_DRIVER` env var (`local` | `s3` | `s3-presigned` | `cloudinary`). Requests for inactive strategies will receive a 404 or module-not-found error.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Upload — Local Storage",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "",
                  "description": "Image file to upload (jpg, jpeg, png, gif)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base}}/files/upload",
              "host": ["{{base}}"],
              "path": ["files", "upload"]
            },
            "description": "Uploads an image to the **local filesystem** (`./uploads/` on the server).\n\nActive when `FILE_DRIVER=local`.\n\nAccepted types: `image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `image/gif`.\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{\n  \"file\": {\n    \"id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"path\": \"<relative-path>\"\n  }\n}\n```"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has file', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('file');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Download — Local Storage",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base}}/files/:path",
              "host": ["{{base}}"],
              "path": ["files", ":path"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "path",
                  "value": "replace-with-file-path-from-upload-response",
                  "description": "The `path` value returned by the Local Upload response"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Downloads/streams a file from local storage by its relative path.\n\nActive when `FILE_DRIVER=local`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Upload — AWS S3",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "",
                  "description": "Image file to upload (jpg, jpeg, png, gif)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base}}/files/upload",
              "host": ["{{base}}"],
              "path": ["files", "upload"]
            },
            "description": "Uploads an image directly to **AWS S3**.\n\nActive when `FILE_DRIVER=s3`.\n\nRequires env vars: `ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_DEFAULT_S3_BUCKET`, `AWS_S3_REGION`.\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{\n  \"file\": {\n    \"id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"path\": \"<s3-object-key>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe Tests script saves `file.id` → `fileId` for use in the **Get Presigned URL** request below."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('File id saved', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('file');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.file).to.have.property('id');",
                  "  pm.environment.set('fileId', json.file.id);",
                  "  console.log('fileId saved:', json.file.id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Presigned URL — AWS S3",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base}}/files/{{fileId}}/url",
              "host": ["{{base}}"],
              "path": ["files", "{{fileId}}", "url"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "expiresIn",
                  "value": "3600",
                  "description": "URL TTL in seconds (default: 3600 = 1 hour)",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns a **presigned GET URL** for the file with the given ID. The URL can be used directly in `<img src>` or downloaded — no Authorization header needed.\n\nActive when `FILE_DRIVER=s3`.\n\nWorks for both **public and private** S3 buckets.\n\nPrerequisite: `fileId` must be set (auto-saved by *Upload — AWS S3* above).\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{ \"url\": \"https://bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/key?X-Amz-...\" }\n```\n\nOptional query param `expiresIn` (seconds) controls how long the URL is valid."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has presigned url', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('url');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.url).to.include('X-Amz-Signature');",
                  "  console.log('Presigned URL:', json.url.substring(0, 80) + '...');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Upload — S3 Presigned URL",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"fileName\": \"my-image.jpg\",\n  \"fileSize\": 204800,\n  \"mimeType\": \"image/jpeg\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base}}/files/upload",
              "host": ["{{base}}"],
              "path": ["files", "upload"]
            },
            "description": "Returns a **presigned S3 URL** that the client must use to PUT the file directly to S3 (server never receives the binary).\n\nActive when `FILE_DRIVER=s3-presigned`.\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{\n  \"file\": { \"id\": \"<uuid>\", \"path\": \"<s3-key>\" },\n  \"uploadSignedUrl\": \"https://...\"\n}\n```\n\nAfter receiving the response, upload the file via:\n```\nPUT {{uploadSignedUrl}}\nContent-Type: image/jpeg\nBody: <binary file>\n```"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has uploadSignedUrl', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('uploadSignedUrl');",
                  "  console.log('Use this URL to PUT your file:', json.uploadSignedUrl);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Upload — Cloudinary",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "",
                  "description": "Image file to upload (jpg, jpeg, png, gif, webp, svg)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base}}/files/upload",
              "host": ["{{base}}"],
              "path": ["files", "upload"]
            },
            "description": "Uploads an image to **Cloudinary**.\n\nActive when `FILE_DRIVER=cloudinary`.\n\nRequires env vars: `CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME`, `CLOUDINARY_API_KEY`, `CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET`.\n\nAccepted types: `image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `image/gif`, `image/webp`, `image/svg+xml`.\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{\n  \"file\": {\n    \"id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"path\": \"https://res.cloudinary.com/<cloud>/<public_id>\"\n  }\n}\n```"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has file', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('file');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
